0334-negroni-bt-qup-clocks: Bluetooth stage A step 4 (QUP2 clocks) as Linux checks them, plus the RPMh BCM QUP2 vote.

Root cause of the stop at step 4 on the phone (logs/usblog-everything-0363.txt, 02:02:43): s_ahb CBCR read
0x80000002 = HW_CTL (bit 1) set + CLK_OFF (bit 31) set. gcc_qupv3_wrap_2_s_ahb_clk and _m_ahb_clk have
hwcg_bit 1 (Linux gcc-sm8450.c); clk-branch.c clk_branch_wait skips the halt check for a branch in hardware
gating mode, because CLK_OFF reads 1 while the AHB is idle. 0330 waited for CLK_OFF = 0 and stopped.
The same pattern stops 0350 (fingerprint, wrap_1_s_ahb CBCR 0x80000002) in the same boot.

negroni_bt.c: cbcr_state() = on / hw-gated / OFF; only OFF stops. Step 4 first votes BCM "QUP2" (Linux
geni_icc_enable "qup-core": qup2_core_master -> qup2_core_slave, bcm_qup2 keepalive, vote_scale 1) with
5000 kBps (qcom-geni-se.h CORE_2X_100_MHZ); failure only logged. Boot-args negronibt_bcm=0 (skip),
negronibt_bcm_kbps=N. negroni_rpmh.c: negroni_rpmh_qup_bcm() (QUP0/1/2 only, bcm-voter.c arithmetic,
never voted off).

